# FizzBuzz — the classic screening question: print 1..N, but multiples of 3
# say Fizz, multiples of 5 say Buzz, and multiples of both say FizzBuzz.
#
# Domain has no range generator, so the program builds 1..15 itself: start
# from [1] and Repeat appending length+1. Divisibility is n/k*k = n
# (integer division), and totext renders the plain numbers.
#
#   domain challenges/01_fizzbuzz.domain
Cursed Energy: 01_fizzbuzz.input
Cursed Technique: Apply
    Using: (s) -> list(toint(s))
Simple Domain: Repeat 14
    Cursed Technique: Apply
        Using: (xs) -> concat(xs, list(length(xs) + 1))
Cursed Technique: Map Each
    Using: (n) -> if n / 15 * 15 = n then "FizzBuzz" else (if n / 3 * 3 = n then "Fizz" else (if n / 5 * 5 = n then "Buzz" else totext(n)))
Maximum Technique: Join with "\n"
Reveal: stdout
